nodecode-escalation-governor is a rewrite of jusst01's jusst01/escalation-governor:

  https://github.com/jusst01/escalation-governor
  commit 50fcf38919b721fe481a60f728bf7271b15b6e82
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 jusst (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole signal engine of governor.py -- the four deterministic
signals with their thresholds, the per-session counters, the reset on a
successful tool result, the once-per-turn injection rule, the recovery rule,
and the packet (trip reason, the goal, every attempt with how it ended) -- and
the parts of __init__.py a cell can carry: the hooks that feed it, the
/escalation-governor command with its status and its report, and the JSONL
report file under the home. The default thresholds keep their original
numbers (3, 3, 3, 12). The section replaces the plugin's JSON file and its
GOVERNOR_* environment variables with typed settings the operator sets in
/settings, and a setting of 0 turns that signal off.

Left out, and why: the hooks Hermes has and Nodecode does not. Hermes'
pre_llm_call and transform_tool_result are one seam here in each direction --
Nodecode's :ROUND point records the packet into the round's request, and the
:TOOL point appends it to the round's next tool result -- so the packet
arrives at both of the moments the original chose. post_tool_call and
api_request_error became the :TOOL point and the advice on the one provider
call a round makes; post_api_request's token accounting is gone, because the
packet needs no token counts and the consideration was never shown to anyone.
subagent_start and subagent_stop have no portable seam in a cell, so a trip
clears on the first successful tool result that follows it, which is the
recovery the original detected too, and the report's delegation flag is
replaced by that same recovery flag. on_session_end appended a report at the
end of a session; a cell has no such event, so a line is appended when a
session trips and when it recovers, and /escalation-governor report reads
the newest of them. The goal was read from the session's first user message;
a cell is not handed the prompt text, so the goal comes from
/escalation-governor goal TEXT, and the packet says where to find it when
it does not.
